    given-names: Tomasz
identifiers: []
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kazulak/relativistic-distributed-systems-sim"
abstract: >-
  A Julia discrete-event simulator for distributed-systems protocols,
  currently Raft consensus, executing on moving worldlines in flat
  (special-relativistic) Minkowski spacetime. It provides a typed physics
  kernel with proper-time clocks and causal light-cone message delivery, a
  protocol-faithful static-membership Raft state machine with runtime
  invariant auditing and client-history linearizability checking, a
  deterministic research scenario harness, and fingerprintable adaptation
  policy tooling.
keywords:
  - raft
  - consensus
  - special-relativity
  - spacetime
  - discrete-event-simulation
  - distributed-systems
  - failure-detection
